# Deliberate search boundary, not an exclusion of the record.
# `docs/archive/` is append-only history: spent reports, retired prompts, session
# logs, settled decision bodies. It is kept OUT of a default ripgrep so a routine
# search returns only what is live — and it is still there, on purpose:
#     rg <term> docs/archive/     search the archive by naming it
#     rg --no-ignore <term>       search live + archive in one pass
# `grep -r` and `git log/grep` ignore this file entirely and always see everything.
# Carried from SMR-BugFixPack 2026-09-17 (docs/agent/PROVENANCE.md §6).
# Full note: docs/README.md -> "The archive boundary".
docs/archive/
